        "Enkhjin stands in the tent door, with her stick, a quarter of his size. She says the girl is hers. Ganbold says the girl is his. They have said it many times. Behind Enkhjin the girl is standing very straight, with her hands clenched, and her lips are moving, as if she were repeating a name that was not Ganbold’s or Enkhjin’s.",
